;;; The twin of `wild-in-head.ein` — M1e2 **W20**, banked by S1e2.2.20
;;; (2026-11-05): the same program with the head wildcard written out as the
;;; disjunction over the relations it has that a one-argument fact can
;;; belong to, `holds` and `hit`. A fresh variable is no twin for a head (M1
;;; binds a relation head by the activator, Q29). Its answer is the
;;; witness's right one: `w` fires on `(holds a)`, root holds `(hit w)`, and
;;; R is `{(hit w)}` and `{(hit a), (hit w)}` (`ein solve FILE` at
;;; `c73a0796`, release and debug).

(relation holds Node) (relation hit Node)
(holds a)
(rule w () :match (or (holds a) (hit a)) :assert (hit w))
